@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+## In `api-server.py`
+
+1. change `pitch2d` in `/predict_prosody_features` and `/generate_prosody`'s
+   request to `pitchHz2d`.
+2. change `pitch2d` in `/predict_prosody_features`'s request to `pitchHz2d`.
+
+`pitch2d` is z-score normalized, while others (with `frequency` in the names)
+are not. You should do the conversion in the endpoints accordingly.
+
+see `plot_mel` in `utils/tools.py` for reference on how to normalize and
+denormalize.
diff --git a/refactoring/instructions/s2/8.md b/refactoring/instructions/s2/8.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b1a2003
--- /dev/null
+++ b/refactoring/instructions/s2/8.md
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+## in `api-server.py`
+
+1. don't accept `*_control` & `speed` anymore in
+   `POST /predict_prosody_features` and `POST /generate_prosody`'s requests.
+2. in `POST /predict_prosody_features`'s requests, move `duration`, `pitch` and
+   `energy` into an optional&nullable object called
+   `featurePredictionOverrides`.
+3. in `POST /generate_prosody`'s requests, move `duration`, `pitch` and `energy`
+   into an optional&nullable object called `featurePredictions`.
+4. in `POST /predict_prosody_features`'s responses, group predictions into
+   different objects with their feature names. (e.g.
+   `{ "duration": { "ticksPerSecond": …, "durationTicks2d": … }, "pitch": { "pitchHz2d": … }, … }`.)
+5. if a feature is overriden in `POST /predict_prosody_features`, instead of
+   responding with the prediction of that feature, respond with
+   `{ "isOverriden": true }`. (for example, if `duration` is provided, the
+   response should look like
+   `{ "duration": { "isOverriden": true }, "pitch": { ... }, "energy": { ... } }`.)
diff --git a/refactoring/instructions/s2/9.md b/refactoring/instructions/s2/9.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6b7a6d1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/refactoring/instructions/s2/9.md
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+## in `api-server.py`
+
+1. make all features in `featurePredictions` and the object itself mandatory in
+   `POST /generate_prosody`'s requests .
+2. add back speed, pitch-control and energy-control to
+   `POST /predict_prosody_features`'s requests. This time, they should be
+   grouped in an object like `{ "speed": …, "pitch": …, "energy": … }`, and the
+   object should be called `controls` and located in the root of the request.
+   `featurePredictionOverrides.duration` and `controls.speed` should be mutually
+   exclusive, same for `pitch` and `energy`.
